cl inlines this case's closure away and emits no symbol for it, where cxx1 emits ??R$_0@?1??main@@9@QEBA_NHH@Z as an ordinary definition - the same difference lambda-after-destructible.nonames records against clang, and the one CLAUDE.md notes for every closure and inline special member: cxx1 has no way to say a definition is mergeable-and-discardable, so it emits what the other compilers fold. It is a difference about emission, not about naming. What this case is about, which object a replayed lambda body destroys, is a run-time question and is checked by run-cases.cmd on the box and by run.sh on the other two.
